    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass, including the new fiscal-year tests (Cp14, Cp48), with a successful build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, identified by its ending calendar year \u2014 e.g. 1 Jul 2026 \u2192 30 Jun 2027 is **FY27**).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Added a `fiscalYear(LocalDate)` helper (July\u2013December \u2192 next calendar year, January\u2013June \u2192 same year).\n- `generateMembershipNumber` now uses the fiscal year's last two digits instead of the calendar year, so the `-M<YY>` segment is fiscal-year-derived from the business-day-adjusted registration date.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Added a `fiscalYear` DTO field via `deriveFiscalYear`, formatting `FY<YY>` from the registration date (falls back to today if absent).\n- Replaced the 365-day `tenureDays` gate with `tenureFiscalYears` (elapsed fiscal years = fiscal year of today \u2212 fiscal year of registration). Membership points now award +3 for one or more elapsed fiscal years. A freshly registered owner still has zero tenure, so all existing membership-level/points tests remain green.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**\n- Added the `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`) response property.\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect fiscal-year semantics.\n\nThe membership number and `fiscalYear` field are internally consistent (both derive from the same adjusted registration date), so for an August 2026 registration the response now reports `fiscalYear: FY27` and a membership number ending `-M27`.",
